      "content": "The civil liberties argument is frequently a cover for political agendas, as it often ignores the overwhelming data showing that unchecked outbreaks cause far more harm than the restrictions themselves. While some concerns about government overreach are valid in theory, they are rendered moot when the alternative is a public health collapse that kills thousands of people. True rationality demands that we accept the science to save lives, rather than using abstract principles to justify preventable tragedy.",
      "source": "target",
